Valtz includes, unmodified, MAGI-2-preview's prompt enhancement
(https://github.com/SandAI-org/MAGI-2-preview, commit
f68a0f9bbccbea56e0177a9bd912abc3b18ffe61, inference/prompt_enhancement):

  prompt_enhancement/prompts/t2v.md
  prompt_enhancement/prompts/i2v.md
  prompt_enhancement/enhancer.py
  prompt_enhancement/pe_markdown.py
  prompt_enhancement/pe_schemas.py

t2v.md and i2v.md are used, as the instructions their makers publish, by
Valtz's prompt enhancer when the target model is MAGI-2-preview: t2v.md
for a clip from words, i2v.md for one opening on a picture, each sent as
enhancer.py sends it -- one message, the request in its place. The
Python files are not run: Valtz renders the reply to Markdown with code
of its own that follows pe_markdown.py (the core's assist::magi2_prompt),
and keeps them here as that code's reference.
